{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Final report — Option A implemented (RED→GREEN), pushed for review\n\n**Gerrit change:** https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2351\n(`refs/for/main`, Change-Id `I1438b9ddbfc471c840044a8759331bf45b4db47d`).\nAwaiting `LLM-Review +1` AND `Verified +1`. Ticket stays `in_progress` until both\nvotes are green and the change is merged.\n\n### The fix (single choke point)\n- Added `rebar._mcp_errors.js_safe_dumps(value, **kwargs)` =\n  `json.dumps(js_safe_result(value), **kwargs)` beside the proven MCP `js_safe_result`.\n- Routed EVERY CLI `--output json` / `--output llm` store-data emitter through it —\n  34 sites across `reads_cli`, `signing`, `_commands/*`, `_cli/*`, `_engine_support/*`\n  — not only the timestamp verbs. An out-of-JS-range int now leaves as its exact\n  decimal STRING; in-range ints/bools/floats/str/null are untouched; conversion is\n  lossless (same digits, different JSON type).\n\n### Reintroduction guard (criterion 1)\n- New AST gate `scripts/check_cli_json_js_safe.py`, wired into `make lint`, FAILS if a\n  CLI emitter writes store data to stdout via a raw `json.dumps`. Sanction marker\n  `# js-safe-ok: <reason>` (mandatory reason). Self-tested in\n  `tests/unit/test_cli_json_js_safe_guard.py` (discrimination, sanction, reasonless\n  marker, unparseable-source loudness, real-tree-clean, `make lint` wiring).\n\n### Declared-int caveat (criterion 2)\n- The CLI path applies the conversion to PLAIN dicts (from `show_state`/`to_llm`/the\n  sign manifest) with NO pydantic `model_validate` afterwards, so the string form does\n  not silently revert to a bare number. Schema already types the fields\n  `[\"integer\",\"string\",\"null\"]`. Verified on the wire.\n\n### Regression test (criterion 3)\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py` (RED-first; confirmed RED for\n  the right reason before the fix). Asserts BOTH (a) `int(wire) == stored` (lossless)\n  AND (b) the wire value is a JSON STRING (the direct BigInt-serialization guard),\n  across `show` json+llm, `list`, and `sign`. Adds an end-to-end Node `BigInt`\n  parse+re-serialize assertion (self-skips when `node` is absent).\n- Mutation-tested the oracle: disabling the conversion → 5 RED; a lossy\n  `str(int(float(value)))` \"fix\" → the exact-round-trip oracle FAILS. Teeth confirmed.\n\n### End-to-end replication (real CLI subprocess)\n```\nSTORED created_at (ns int): 1787957157590831001  (19 digits)\nWIRE token:                 \"1787957157590831001\"   ← quoted string\nNode BigInt parse:          1787957157590831001  → re-serialized OK (no TypeError)\njq .created_at:             1787957157590831001  (exact; no float64 rounding)\n```\n\n### Gates (all green locally)\n`make lint` (incl. the new gate) · `make typecheck` (684 files) · complexity ratchet\n(new=0 increased=0) · module-size (all <800) · `probe_rebar` (142/0) ·\n`tests/interfaces` facades+contracts tier (1005 passed) · regression+guard suites (26).\n\n### Docs\nBREAKING (pre-1.0) entries added to `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`,\nper-surface, superseding the MCP entry's \"CLI `--output json` … UNCHANGED\" note;\n`int()`/`BigInt()` consumers unaffected.\n\n### Plan-review gate\n`review-plan` verdict **PASS** (0 blocking; 3 advisory). Advisory on the Node-test\navailability precondition was addressed by adding the `shutil.which(\"node\")` skip guard.\nAttestation certified (`verified_at_sha 2598909d…`).\n\n### Close plan\nClose with `--class=preexisting`, NO `--caused-by`, only AFTER `Verified +1` and merge."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787958585997521001,"uuid":"f07ef6aa-4e17-46bc-bf8d-dda9d688b59a"}